{"kind":"event","event_id":1852,"event_uid":"01M2HAYDY4AV4PCDG1TT9T3HF4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":105,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW49P05CV8CEQ1VFZT4D4","issue_short_id":"t4d4","actor":"impl:2@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435787204,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"a508a890a0be9cf87b4bac6358dca11df435b954cfd4e36d0b7c43365247bcf6","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAYDY39S79J3H71XGVVYF0","author":"impl:2@run-131","body":"task 2 approach: kataProjectFor(target) -> one project per target; kata-client gains Idempotency-Key on createIssue and replace on link, purgeProject deleted; fileRunOnHub does create(key)->getIssue->patchMetadata({run,wave,factsheet},rev)->parent link replace:true, then blocks links; pushPlan's bump closes run-N wontfix instead of purging. Plan blob sha computed in-process with createHash('sha1').","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:29:47.203057147Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:29:47.204Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1853,"event_uid":"01M2HAYWX9B136T4CRVX2G1GA4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":106,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW59W6RCFBRQ77F472S0K","issue_short_id":"2s0k","actor":"impl:3@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435802537,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"38094466a845d9aefc007c0d459467f97f7e5e4f4776cdcb27fc4f29fc8985da","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAYWX8KSHXKFZ0D0EPAVYH","author":"impl:3@run-131","body":"Task 3: janitor hub reader looks up the project by kataProjectFor(target) = <owner>-<repo>. Plan: (1) lobby.mjs:212 kataProjectFor drops the run arg and the -run-<N> suffix, comment rewritten; (2) janitor.mjs:332 calls it with target only, and the module doc at ~20 says the target's one project; (3) CONTRACT.md's janitor row says \"matched on \\`name\\` against the target's one project \\`<owner>-<repo>\\`\". Touching only the janitor row in CONTRACT.md (sibling task 2 owns the launcher row).","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:02.536260317Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:02.537Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1854,"event_uid":"01M2HAYY47KMSNJ88J8CPM0B8M","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":107,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW69108NJKD6VZ81CN48T","issue_short_id":"n48t","actor":"impl:4@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435803783,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b999646a62df9f14611012b7e914d1c48fe4277e188ee445cce83f65e3bef516","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAYY46XJTVZST5TV16DB4V","author":"impl:4@run-131","body":"Task 4 approach: extend `kata_assemble` in fleet/sandbox-boot.sh to take $KATA_FILE as its first argument, build the keep-set from `run.uid` plus every `tasks.<id>.uid`, and filter issues on `uid` and events on `issue_uid` (an event with no `issue_uid`, e.g. `project.created`, is dropped). The paging loop, the temp-name-then-mv and the 'previous kept' failure branches are untouched. CONTRACT.md's `kata.jsonl` bullet is reworded to carry 'the run's issues' / 'named by' / 'events on them' in that order. The exam at fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_kata_export.mjs is the peer's; I write none.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:03.782406487Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:03.783Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1855,"event_uid":"01M2HAZG1M5KJ56C17H0MEKSRS","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":104,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW3B85YJD5G0N2W7RN6Y2","issue_short_id":"n6y2","actor":"exam:1@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435822132,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"f2bbeb533ba13a6d679e12e80103bae003e243784c6c63871edd3460ac54d194","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAZG1J375SQP5128Q1VKQA","author":"exam:1@run-131","body":"examiner (task 1): writing tests/test_compile_plan_edges.py in the shape of tests/test_review_peer.py — small claims-v1 plans written to tmp_path, compiler run as a subprocess, stdout JSON parsed for dag_edges/waves. Legs a–d each get their own plan fixture built from a shared builder so the header/slot grammar is written once; leg e is two scoped greps over skills/ultrawrite/SKILL.md matching the Proof's own sed|tr|grep commands. First step is to validate every fixture plan compiles clean at BASE (PLAN OK, no grammar violations) so the exam's only red at BASE is the absent proof-run tier and the absent Check refusal.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:22.130708769Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:22.132Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1856,"event_uid":"01M2HAZM4H7H6YDRJPEABF4SMS","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":107,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW69108NJKD6VZ81CN48T","issue_short_id":"n48t","actor":"exam:4@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435826321,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"efabdddb30ef4cb900c15d8f52ab00f5050b407781b0c6effab5e219326cc1ec","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAZM4GDA97P486VYMW53E0","author":"exam:4@run-131","body":"examiner (task 4): writing `fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_kata_export.mjs` against M1–M4.\n\nApproach: four legs, at most three boots, all driven through `_sandbox_boot_helpers.mjs`.\n- One boot with `STUB_KATA_JSON` naming run uid `R7` + task uids `T1`,`T2` (the Global-Constraints record shape), `STUB_KATA_ISSUES` answering `R7,T1,T2,X9` and `STUB_KATA_EVENTS` answering project.created (no `issue_uid`) then events on `T1,X9,R7,T2`. Legs (a) and (b) read `kataJsonl(ctx)` off that one boot: issue lines exactly `R7,T1,T2` in hub order, event lines exactly the `T1,R7,T2` envelopes in log order.\n- Leg (c) splits: the paging half reads the recorded curl argv of that same green boot (every export asks `after_id=0` then the stub's `next_after_id` and no third cursor); the failure half is a second boot with `STUB_KATA_ISSUES_EXIT_FROM=2` + a non-zero `STUB_KATA_ISSUES_EXIT` (the rig's exit knob defaults to 0, so `_FROM` alone fails nothing), asserting the landed `kata.jsonl` is byte-equal to the first export's filtered text while the issues endpoint was asked more than once.\n- Leg (d) runs the Proof's own `Run:` sed/grep over `fleet/CONTRACT.md` in-process, plus the three words in order.\n\nExpect red at BASE for one reason: `kata_assemble` filters nothing, so `X9` and the project event ride the export.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:26.320300230Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:26.321Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1857,"event_uid":"01M2HAZRB9PPCR7RTEZM9M17R4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131","issue_id":104,"issue_uid":"01M2HAW3B85YJD5G0N2W7RN6Y2","issue_short_id":"n6y2","actor":"impl:1@run-131","hlc_physical_ms":1789435830633,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b7787a8e2864390183b698c624e815e62d808601e37dff17a8cc08423ebdefa4","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HAZRB8F54NVD6WPKFMQ759","author":"impl:1@run-131","body":"task 1 approach: add a `proof-run` edge tier to build_edges between the interface tier and non-text-overlap (so an interface edge already in `seen` wins), keyed on a whole-token regex match of each task's Proof `Run:` commands against every other implementation task's four Files sets, skipping paths the running task itself owns. Separately, under --check only, a run-wide `- Check:` command naming a path an implementation task's Files own becomes a grammar violation naming the task id and the path. Then two plain sentences in skills/ultrawrite/SKILL.md (Task shape, Global Constraints discipline).","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:30.632846847Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:30:30.633Z"}
